# Strategy B (REALTIME_MOMENTUM_V1) FSM/setup/entry/exit rules checksum.
#
# canonical: sha256 of json.dumps(payload, sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":"), ensure_ascii=False) UTF-8
#            = app.backtest.strategy_c_selection.rules.canonical_checksum (existing US-B recipe)
# file:      sha256 of the file bytes (informational; the canonical value is the gate)
#
# declared:  2026-09-20 20:45 KST (current), repo main at 3793bd1
# results:   0. No B backtest has been run against data. Every draft below was superseded while the
#            implementation was being written, before any B result existed, which is what makes the
#            supersessions legitimate rather than post-hoc rule fitting.
#
# history (each line: the checksum that was replaced, and why)
#   2026-09-19 18:51  d6063e17024df2fd79a1eb475ca46ef918e7bf333719d8688eb577d9a6e297ff
#       SETUP_READY became a per-tick re-evaluation: the trigger is judged before the close-below-stop
#       invalidation (a bar that breaks out and then fails is a taken loss, not a cancelled setup), a
#       setup that merely disappears falls back to WATCHING, and the signal-then-fill tick order was
#       written down.
#   2026-09-19 19:05  94d5a13689d0438dc101b4c68582ad0b11bf1aa4afb94e5fc796c7903549e928
#       Eligibility is rechecked in every non-terminal state and ahead of the TTL check, so an
#       ENTRY_SIGNALLED candidate can still be REJECTED when a halt is inferred.
#   2026-09-19 19:09  288cd7e308393e52b23e82518d185d0c46ce5cbdd73a7316cd2160d89097760c
#       The exit layer was implemented: the exit scan starts at the entry bar, HARD_STOP vs
#       TRAILING_STOP is decided by whether the stop has moved, a partial that rounds to zero shares
#       closes the whole position at the target, a deadline fills at the last close before it, sizing
#       only lowers for the position cap, and CON is recorded as a universe exclusion.
#   2026-09-20 20:45  54c6063015999ac56d33c69c21d1463e68d9727c13d65c3ff8d47db3ec5e2c13
#       The session engine found a calendar hole: 15:55 falls after the bell on an early-close
#       session, so the EOD exit is clamped to regular_close - eod_min_margin_minutes (5). That is
#       15:55 on a standard day and keeps the rule meaningful on a half day.
